var e=`penflow-finding-templates`,t=1,n=`en`,r=[{id:`cleartext-ftp`,language:`en`,title:`Cleartext FTP service`,description:`The host offers FTP without TLS. Credentials and file contents travel unencrypted, so anyone able to observe the traffic between the client and the server can read or alter them.`,impact:`An attacker on the same network path can capture valid credentials and the files transferred, and reuse those credentials against this or other systems.`,remediation:`- Replace FTP with SFTP, or require explicit TLS (FTPS) for every session.
- If FTP must stay, restrict it to trusted networks and to accounts that are not used elsewhere.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`cleartext`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ftp-cleartext`],version:1},{id:`cleartext-telnet`,language:`en`,title:`Telnet service in use`,description:`The host exposes a Telnet service. Telnet sends the whole session, credentials included, in cleartext and offers no way to verify the server.`,impact:`Captured credentials give interactive access to the device, often with administrative privileges.`,remediation:`- Disable Telnet and use SSH for remote administration.
- Limit management interfaces to a dedicated administration network.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`cleartext`,`management`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:telnet-exposed`],version:1},{id:`cleartext-http`,language:`en`,title:`Web service without TLS`,description:`The application is served over plain HTTP. Requests and responses, including session cookies and anything typed into forms, can be read and modified in transit.`,impact:`An attacker on the network path can steal sessions or credentials and inject content into the pages users receive.`,remediation:`- Serve the application only over HTTPS and redirect HTTP to it.
- Enable HTTP Strict Transport Security once HTTPS works everywhere.`,references:[`WSTG-CRYP-03`],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`cleartext`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-no-tls`],version:1},{id:`cleartext-mail`,language:`en`,title:`Mail service without encryption`,description:`A mail service (POP3, IMAP or SMTP submission) accepts connections without TLS, so mailbox credentials and messages can be sent in cleartext.`,impact:`Captured credentials give access to mailboxes, which commonly hold password reset links and sensitive correspondence.`,remediation:`- Require TLS on every mail protocol (implicit TLS or mandatory STARTTLS) and refuse authentication over unencrypted sessions.`,references:[`RFC 8314`],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`mail`,`cleartext`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:mail-cleartext`],version:1},{id:`smtp-no-starttls`,language:`en`,title:`SMTP server does not offer STARTTLS`,description:`The SMTP server does not announce STARTTLS. Messages exchanged with other mail servers travel unencrypted.`,impact:`Messages and their attachments can be read or altered by anyone on the network path between mail servers.`,remediation:`- Enable STARTTLS with a valid certificate.
- Consider MTA-STS so that sending servers require encryption.`,references:[`RFC 3207`,`RFC 8461`],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`low`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`mail`,`cleartext`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:smtp-no-starttls`],version:1},{id:`snmp-v1-v2c`,language:`en`,title:`SNMP v1/v2c in use`,description:`The device answers SNMP version 1 or 2c. These versions authenticate with a community string sent in cleartext and do not encrypt the data exchanged.`,impact:`Anyone who learns the community string can read the device configuration and, with a write community, change it.`,remediation:`- Migrate to SNMPv3 with authentication and privacy (authPriv).
- Restrict SNMP to the management network and to known managers.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`management`,`cleartext`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:snmp-exposed`],version:1},{id:`snmp-default-community`,language:`en`,title:`SNMP default community string`,description:`The device accepts a default or well-known SNMP community string such as "public" or "private".`,impact:`An attacker can enumerate the device configuration, interfaces and routes and, if write access is granted, change the configuration.`,remediation:`- Remove default communities and set long random ones, or move to SNMPv3.
- Limit which hosts may query SNMP.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1392`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`management`,`default-credentials`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:snmp-default-community`],version:1},{id:`database-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`Database service reachable from untrusted networks`,description:`A database server accepts connections from networks that should not reach it directly. Databases are meant to be reached only by the applications that use them.`,impact:`Exposure enables password guessing, exploitation of database vulnerabilities and, if authentication is weak, direct access to the data.`,remediation:`- Allow connections only from the application servers that need them (firewall and listen address).
- Require strong authentication and TLS for every connection.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`database`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:mysql-exposed`,`vnmap:postgresql-exposed`,`vnmap:mssql-exposed`],version:1},{id:`datastore-no-auth`,language:`en`,title:`Data store without authentication`,description:`A data store (for example Redis, MongoDB, Elasticsearch or Memcached) can be used without credentials from the network.`,impact:`Anyone who reaches it can read, change or delete its data, and some of these services allow writing files or running commands on the host.`,remediation:`- Enable authentication and authorisation on the service.
- Bind it to local or internal interfaces only, and filter access by firewall.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-306`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`database`,`authentication`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:redis-exposed`,`vnmap:mongodb-exposed`,`vnmap:elasticsearch-exposed`,`vnmap:memcached-exposed`],version:1},{id:`ldap-anonymous`,language:`en`,title:`LDAP anonymous queries allowed`,description:`The directory accepts anonymous binds that can search its contents.`,impact:`An unauthenticated attacker can list users, groups and other directory objects, which helps to target password guessing and phishing.`,remediation:`- Disable anonymous binds or limit them to the RootDSE.
- Require authenticated, encrypted (LDAPS or StartTLS) binds for searches.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1188`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`directory`,`authentication`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ldap-anonymous-search`],version:1},{id:`ldap-rootdse`,language:`en`,title:`LDAP RootDSE readable without authentication`,description:`The directory answers RootDSE queries without authentication, revealing its naming contexts, supported features and sometimes host names.`,impact:`The information helps an attacker map the directory and the domain before attacking it.`,remediation:`- If the RootDSE does not need to be public, restrict anonymous access to it.
- Treat the disclosed information as known to attackers.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-497`],defaultSeverity:`info`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`directory`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ldap-rootdse-readable`],version:1},{id:`dns-open-resolver`,language:`en`,title:`Open DNS resolver`,description:`The DNS server resolves recursive queries for any client, not only for the networks it serves.`,impact:`It can be abused to amplify denial of service attacks against third parties and to poison its cache.`,remediation:`- Restrict recursion to internal clients, or disable it on authoritative servers.
- Apply response rate limiting.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-406`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:L`},tags:[`network`,`dns`,`denial-of-service`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:dns-recursion-allowed`],version:1},{id:`ntp-monlist`,language:`en`,title:`NTP monlist enabled`,description:`The NTP server answers the "monlist" command, which returns a large response to a small request.`,impact:`The server can be used to amplify denial of service attacks against third parties.`,remediation:`- Update the NTP software and disable monlist (for example with "disable monitor").
- Restrict NTP queries to the clients that need them.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-406`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:L`},tags:[`network`,`denial-of-service`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ntp-monlist-enabled`],version:1},{id:`smb-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`SMB service reachable from untrusted networks`,description:`File sharing over SMB is reachable from networks that should not access it.`,impact:`Exposed SMB is a frequent target of password guessing, relay attacks and exploitation of SMB vulnerabilities.`,remediation:`- Block SMB (TCP 445 and 139) at the perimeter and between segments that do not need it.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`network`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:smb-exposed`],version:1},{id:`smbv1-enabled`,language:`en`,title:`SMBv1 protocol enabled`,description:`The server still accepts the obsolete SMBv1 protocol, which lacks the security improvements of later versions.`,impact:`SMBv1 has been the vector of wormable remote code execution vulnerabilities and allows downgrade attacks.`,remediation:`- Disable SMBv1 on servers and clients after checking that no legacy system depends on it.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-477`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`network`,`obsolete`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:smbv1-enabled`],version:1},{id:`smb-signing`,language:`en`,title:`SMB signing not required`,description:`The server does not require SMB message signing.`,impact:`An attacker who can intercept or relay authentication can forward it to this host and act with the victim's privileges (NTLM relay).`,remediation:`- Require SMB signing on servers and clients through policy.
- Reduce NTLM use and enable Extended Protection for Authentication where available.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-347`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`active-directory`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:smb-signing-not-required`],version:1},{id:`smb-null-session`,language:`en`,title:`SMB null session allowed`,description:`The server accepts anonymous (null) SMB sessions that can query information such as users, groups or shares.`,impact:`Unauthenticated enumeration helps an attacker prepare password guessing and further attacks.`,remediation:`- Restrict anonymous access through policy (RestrictAnonymous and related settings) and disable guest access.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-306`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`authentication`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:smb-null-session`],version:1},{id:`nfs-world-export`,language:`en`,title:`NFS export available to any host`,description:`An NFS export can be mounted by any host instead of a defined list of clients.`,impact:`An attacker can mount the share and read or modify its files, impersonating local users when root squashing is disabled.`,remediation:`- Restrict each export to the client hosts that need it and enable root squashing.
- Use NFSv4 with Kerberos where possible.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-732`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`file-sharing`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:nfs-export-world`,`vnmap:nfs-exposed`],version:1},{id:`ftp-anonymous`,language:`en`,title:`Anonymous FTP access`,description:`The FTP server accepts anonymous logins.`,impact:`Anyone can list and download the files offered, and upload files if writing is allowed.`,remediation:`- Disable anonymous access unless it is required, and never allow anonymous writes.
- Review the files that are reachable anonymously.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-552`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`file-sharing`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ftp-anonymous`],version:1},{id:`rdp-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`Remote Desktop exposed to untrusted networks`,description:`Remote Desktop (RDP) is reachable from networks that should not reach it, such as the Internet.`,impact:`Exposed RDP is a common entry point through password guessing and through RDP vulnerabilities.`,remediation:`- Reach RDP only through a VPN or a remote desktop gateway with multi-factor authentication.
- Enable Network Level Authentication and account lockout.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`remote-access`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:rdp-exposed`],version:1},{id:`vnc-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`VNC exposed to untrusted networks`,description:`A VNC server is reachable from untrusted networks. VNC often relies on a single password and does not encrypt the session.`,impact:`An attacker who guesses or captures the password gets full control of the desktop.`,remediation:`- Remove the exposure, or tunnel VNC through SSH or a VPN.
- Use strong, unique passwords and, where available, encrypted VNC.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`remote-access`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:vnc-exposed`],version:1},{id:`winrm-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`WinRM reachable from untrusted networks`,description:`Windows Remote Management is reachable from networks that do not need to administer the host.`,impact:`With valid credentials an attacker can run commands remotely; exposure also enables password guessing.`,remediation:`- Allow WinRM only from administration hosts, preferably over HTTPS.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`management`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:winrm-exposed`],version:1},{id:`ssh-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`SSH administration exposed to untrusted networks`,description:`SSH is reachable from networks that do not need to administer the host.`,impact:`Exposure enables password guessing and gives a target to any SSH vulnerability.`,remediation:`- Restrict SSH to administration networks or a bastion host.
- Disable password authentication in favour of keys, and disable direct root login.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`low`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`remote-access`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ssh-exposed`],version:1},{id:`ssh-weak-algorithms`,language:`en`,title:`SSH weak algorithms supported`,description:`The SSH server offers weak key exchange, cipher or MAC algorithms (for example SHA-1 based key exchange, CBC mode ciphers or MD5 MACs).`,impact:`Weak algorithms reduce the protection of administrative sessions and may allow downgrade attacks.`,remediation:`- Configure only current algorithms (for example curve25519 key exchange, AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 ciphers and SHA-2 MACs).`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-327`],defaultSeverity:`low`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`remote-access`,`cryptography`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ssh-weak-algorithms`],version:1},{id:`ipmi-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`IPMI interface reachable from untrusted networks`,description:`The baseboard management controller (IPMI) of the server is reachable outside a dedicated management network.`,impact:`IPMI allows full control of the hardware, and IPMI 2.0 discloses password hashes to unauthenticated requests (RAKP).`,remediation:`- Place management controllers on an isolated management network.
- Disable IPMI over LAN if it is not used, and use unique strong passwords.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`management`,`hardware`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:ipmi-exposed`],version:1},{id:`docker-api`,language:`en`,title:`Docker API exposed without authentication`,description:`The Docker daemon API listens on a network port without TLS client authentication.`,impact:`Anyone who reaches it can start privileged containers and take full control of the host.`,remediation:`- Do not expose the Docker socket on the network; if remote access is needed, require mutual TLS.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-306`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H`},tags:[`containers`,`authentication`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:docker-api-exposed`],version:1},{id:`kubernetes-api`,language:`en`,title:`Kubernetes API server reachable from untrusted networks`,description:`The Kubernetes API server is reachable from networks that should not manage the cluster.`,impact:`Exposure enables attacks on authentication and, with any anonymous or weak access, control of the cluster workloads.`,remediation:`- Restrict access to the API server to administration networks.
- Disable anonymous access and review role bindings.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H`},tags:[`containers`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:kubernetes-api-exposed`],version:1},{id:`etcd-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`etcd reachable without client authentication`,description:`The etcd key-value store answers without client certificate authentication.`,impact:`etcd often holds cluster secrets; reading or writing it can compromise the whole cluster.`,remediation:`- Require mutual TLS for every client and restrict access to the control plane.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-306`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`containers`,`authentication`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:etcd-exposed`],version:1},{id:`ics-protocol-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`Industrial control protocol reachable from untrusted networks`,description:`An industrial protocol such as Modbus, S7 or BACnet is reachable outside the control network. These protocols commonly have no authentication.`,impact:`An attacker can read process values and send commands that change the physical process.`,remediation:`- Isolate control networks and allow these protocols only from the systems that operate the process.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-306`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H`},tags:[`industrial`,`authentication`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:modbus-exposed`,`vnmap:s7-exposed`,`vnmap:bacnet-exposed`],version:1},{id:`admin-interface-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`Administrative web interface exposed`,description:`An administrative web interface is reachable from networks whose users do not need it.`,impact:`Exposed administration panels attract password guessing and exploitation of their vulnerabilities.`,remediation:`- Restrict administration interfaces to administration networks or a VPN, and require multi-factor authentication.`,references:[`WSTG-CONF-05`],cweIds:[`CWE-1327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`management`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:web-admin-panel`],version:1},{id:`default-credentials`,language:`en`,title:`Default credentials accepted`,description:`The service accepts the default credentials of its vendor.`,impact:`Anyone who knows the product can log in with the privileges of that account.`,remediation:`- Change every default password to a unique strong one and disable unused default accounts.
- Check the rest of the estate for the same product.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHN-02`],cweIds:[`CWE-1392`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`,`default-credentials`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-default-credentials`],version:1},{id:`git-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`Version control repository exposed`,description:`The web server serves the contents of a .git directory.`,impact:`An attacker can rebuild the source code, its history and any secrets committed to it.`,remediation:`- Remove version control metadata from the web root and block access to it in the server configuration.
- Rotate any secret found in the repository history.`,references:[`WSTG-CONF-04`],cweIds:[`CWE-527`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-git-exposed`],version:1},{id:`directory-listing`,language:`en`,title:`Directory listing enabled`,description:`The web server lists the contents of directories that have no index page.`,impact:`Listings reveal files that were not meant to be found, such as backups, logs or configuration files.`,remediation:`- Disable directory listing in the server configuration.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-548`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-directory-listing`],version:1},{id:`risky-http-methods`,language:`en`,title:`Dangerous HTTP methods enabled`,description:`The server accepts HTTP methods such as PUT or DELETE on resources where they are not needed.`,impact:`Depending on the server, they may allow uploading or deleting files without proper authorisation.`,remediation:`- Allow only the methods the application uses, and require authorisation for any method that changes content.`,references:[`WSTG-CONF-06`],cweIds:[`CWE-749`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`configuration`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-risky-methods`],version:1},{id:`http-trace`,language:`en`,title:`HTTP TRACE method enabled`,description:`The server answers TRACE requests by echoing them back, headers included.`,impact:`Combined with other flaws it can expose headers such as cookies (cross-site tracing); on its own the risk is low.`,remediation:`- Disable the TRACE method in the web server or proxy.`,references:[`WSTG-CONF-06`],cweIds:[`CWE-489`],defaultSeverity:`low`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`configuration`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-trace-enabled`],version:1},{id:`sensitive-files`,language:`en`,title:`Sensitive files reachable on the web server`,description:`Files that should not be public, such as backups, configuration files, logs or test pages, can be downloaded from the web server.`,impact:`They may reveal credentials, internal paths and details that help further attacks.`,remediation:`- Remove the files from the web root and block similar paths.
- Rotate any credential they contain.`,references:[`WSTG-CONF-04`],cweIds:[`CWE-538`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:http-enum-paths`],version:1},{id:`version-disclosure`,language:`en`,title:`Software version disclosed`,description:`The service reveals its product name and exact version in banners or headers.`,impact:`It helps attackers find vulnerabilities that apply to that version; it is not a vulnerability by itself.`,remediation:`- Reduce banners and headers to what is needed, and keep the software up to date.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-497`],defaultSeverity:`info`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:versioned-service`],version:1},{id:`tls-obsolete-protocols`,language:`en`,title:`Obsolete SSL/TLS protocol versions enabled`,description:`The service accepts SSL 3.0, TLS 1.0 or TLS 1.1, which are deprecated.`,impact:`Obsolete versions rely on weak constructions and allow attacks that can recover parts of the encrypted traffic.`,remediation:`- Allow only TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3.`,references:[`RFC 8996`,`WSTG-CRYP-01`],cweIds:[`CWE-757`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`tls`,`cryptography`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:tls-obsolete-protocol`],version:1},{id:`tls-weak-ciphers`,language:`en`,title:`Weak TLS cipher suites supported`,description:`The service negotiates weak cipher suites, such as RC4, 3DES, export-grade or suites without forward secrecy.`,impact:`Weak suites lower the protection of the connection and may let an attacker decrypt captured traffic.`,remediation:`- Offer only modern AEAD suites with forward secrecy (ECDHE with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305).`,references:[`RFC 9325`,`WSTG-CRYP-01`],cweIds:[`CWE-327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`tls`,`cryptography`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:tls-weak-ciphers`],version:1},{id:`tls-cert-expired`,language:`en`,title:`Expired TLS certificate`,description:`The certificate presented by the service has expired.`,impact:`Clients show errors that users learn to ignore, which makes interception attacks easier; automated clients may fail.`,remediation:`- Renew the certificate and automate renewal and its monitoring.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-324`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`tls`,`certificates`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:tls-cert-expired`],version:1},{id:`tls-cert-untrusted`,language:`en`,title:`Self-signed or untrusted TLS certificate`,description:`The service presents a certificate that is self-signed or issued by an authority clients do not trust.`,impact:`Users cannot tell the genuine service from an impostor, so they are trained to accept certificate warnings.`,remediation:`- Use a certificate issued by a trusted public or internal authority whose root is deployed to the clients.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-295`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`tls`,`certificates`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:tls-cert-self-signed`],version:1},{id:`tls-cert-expiring`,language:`en`,title:`TLS certificate about to expire`,description:`The certificate presented by the service expires soon.`,impact:`If it is not renewed in time, clients will reject the service or warn their users.`,remediation:`- Renew the certificate before it expires and monitor expiry dates.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-324`],defaultSeverity:`info`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`tls`,`certificates`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:tls-cert-expiring-soon`],version:1},{id:`hsts-missing`,language:`en`,title:`HTTP Strict Transport Security not enabled`,description:`The HTTPS application does not send a Strict-Transport-Security header.`,impact:`Users who start from an HTTP link can be kept on HTTP by an attacker on the network (SSL stripping).`,remediation:`- Send Strict-Transport-Security with a long max-age and includeSubDomains once every subdomain supports HTTPS.`,references:[`RFC 6797`,`WSTG-CONF-07`],cweIds:[`CWE-319`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`tls`,`headers`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`unsupported-os`,language:`en`,title:`Operating system no longer supported`,description:`The host runs an operating system version that no longer receives security updates from its vendor.`,impact:`Vulnerabilities found after the end of support remain unpatched and are often exploited.`,remediation:`- Upgrade to a supported version, or isolate the host and plan its replacement.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1104`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`maintenance`,`obsolete`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:windows-unsupported-os`],version:1},{id:`known-vulnerable-version`,language:`en`,title:`Software with known vulnerabilities`,description:`The service runs a version affected by publicly known vulnerabilities.`,impact:`Public vulnerabilities often have exploits available; the impact depends on each one and should be verified.`,remediation:`- Update to a fixed version, or apply the vendor's mitigations until it can be updated.
- Record the CVE identifiers that apply in the references.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1395`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`maintenance`,`cve`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:vulners-cves`,`vnmap:vuln-script-port`,`vnmap:vuln-script-host`],version:1},{id:`vulnerable-client-library`,language:`en`,title:`Client-side library with known vulnerabilities`,description:`The application loads a JavaScript library version affected by publicly known vulnerabilities.`,impact:`Depending on how the library is used, the flaws may allow cross-site scripting or other client-side attacks.`,remediation:`- Update the library to a fixed version and keep an inventory of front-end dependencies.`,references:[`WSTG-INFO-08`],cweIds:[`CWE-1395`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`maintenance`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`sql-injection`,language:`en`,title:`SQL injection`,description:`User input is placed into SQL statements without being handled as data, so it can change the structure of the query.`,impact:`An attacker can read or modify data in the database, bypass authentication and, depending on the database, run commands on the server.`,remediation:`- Use parameterised queries or prepared statements for every query.
- Run the application with a database account that has only the privileges it needs.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-05`,`A03:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-89`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`os-command-injection`,language:`en`,title:`OS command injection`,description:`User input reaches an operating system command without proper neutralisation.`,impact:`An attacker can run arbitrary commands on the server with the privileges of the application.`,remediation:`- Avoid calling the shell; use library functions or pass arguments as a list without a shell.
- Validate input against a strict allow-list.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-12`,`A03:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-78`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`code-injection`,language:`en`,title:`Server-side code injection`,description:`User input is evaluated as code by the application (for example through eval-like functions).`,impact:`An attacker can run arbitrary code in the context of the application.`,remediation:`- Never evaluate user input as code; use safe parsers or data-driven logic instead.`,references:[`A03:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-94`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`ssti`,language:`en`,title:`Server-side template injection`,description:`User input is inserted into a server-side template as template code rather than as data.`,impact:`Template engines often allow reaching the runtime, leading to data disclosure or code execution on the server.`,remediation:`- Pass user input to templates only as variables, never as template source.
- Use a sandboxed template mode where the engine offers one.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-18`],cweIds:[`CWE-1336`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`xxe`,language:`en`,title:`XML external entity (XXE) processing`,description:`The XML parser resolves external entities in documents supplied by users.`,impact:`An attacker can read local files, reach internal services from the server and cause denial of service.`,remediation:`- Disable DTDs and external entity resolution in every XML parser that handles untrusted input.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-07`],cweIds:[`CWE-611`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`,`xml`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`ldap-injection`,language:`en`,title:`LDAP injection`,description:`User input is placed into LDAP filters without escaping.`,impact:`An attacker can alter directory queries to bypass authentication or read entries they should not see.`,remediation:`- Escape special characters in filter values and use parameterised APIs where available.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-06`],cweIds:[`CWE-90`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`,`directory`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`xss-reflected`,language:`en`,title:`Reflected cross-site scripting`,description:`Input from the request is returned in the response without proper output encoding, so a crafted link runs script in the victim's browser.`,impact:`An attacker who gets a user to open a link can act in the application as that user, steal data shown to them or change what they see.`,remediation:`- Encode output for the context where it is placed (HTML, attribute, JavaScript, URL).
- Add a restrictive Content Security Policy as defence in depth.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-01`,`A03:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-79`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`xss`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`xss-stored`,language:`en`,title:`Stored cross-site scripting`,description:`Content stored by one user is later shown to others without proper output encoding, so script runs in their browsers.`,impact:`Every user who views the content is affected; script can act with their sessions, including administrators.`,remediation:`- Encode stored content on output for its context, and sanitise rich text with a maintained library.
- Add a restrictive Content Security Policy as defence in depth.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-02`,`A03:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-79`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`xss`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`xss-dom`,language:`en`,title:`DOM-based cross-site scripting`,description:`Client-side script writes data controlled by an attacker (for example from the URL) into the page in an unsafe way.`,impact:`A crafted link runs script in the victim's browser within the application.`,remediation:`- Use safe DOM APIs such as textContent instead of innerHTML, and avoid passing untrusted data to code-evaluating functions.`,references:[`WSTG-CLNT-01`],cweIds:[`CWE-79`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`xss`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`header-injection`,language:`en`,title:`HTTP response header injection`,description:`User input containing line breaks is placed in response headers.`,impact:`An attacker can add headers or split the response, enabling cache poisoning or cross-site scripting.`,remediation:`- Reject or remove carriage return and line feed characters from values written to headers.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-15`],cweIds:[`CWE-113`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`path-traversal`,language:`en`,title:`Path traversal`,description:`A file path built from user input can leave the intended directory using sequences such as "../".`,impact:`An attacker can read, and in some cases write, files outside the intended directory, including configuration and credentials.`,remediation:`- Map user choices to identifiers instead of paths, or resolve the path and check that it stays inside the allowed directory.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHZ-01`],cweIds:[`CWE-22`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`files`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`file-upload`,language:`en`,title:`Unrestricted file upload`,description:`The application accepts uploaded files without restricting their type or how they are stored and served.`,impact:`An attacker may upload a file that the server executes, or content that attacks other users.`,remediation:`- Allow only the types needed, checked by content, store uploads outside the web root with generated names, and serve them with a safe content type.`,references:[`WSTG-BUSL-09`],cweIds:[`CWE-434`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`files`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`ssrf`,language:`en`,title:`Server-side request forgery`,description:`The application fetches a URL supplied by the user from the server.`,impact:`An attacker can make the server reach internal services or cloud metadata endpoints that are not reachable from outside.`,remediation:`- Allow only the destinations needed (allow-list), resolve and check addresses before connecting, and block internal ranges and metadata endpoints.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-19`,`A10:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-918`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`ssrf`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`open-redirect`,language:`en`,title:`Open redirect`,description:`The application redirects to a URL taken from the request without checking it.`,impact:`Attackers can use links on the trusted domain to send users to malicious sites, which helps phishing and token theft.`,remediation:`- Redirect only to relative paths or to an allow-list of destinations.`,references:[`WSTG-CLNT-04`],cweIds:[`CWE-601`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N`},tags:[`web`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`insecure-deserialization`,language:`en`,title:`Deserialization of untrusted data`,description:`The application deserialises data controlled by the user with a mechanism that can create arbitrary objects.`,impact:`Crafted input can lead to remote code execution or to tampering with application state.`,remediation:`- Do not deserialise untrusted data with native object serialisation; use simple data formats and validate them, or sign the data.`,references:[`A08:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-502`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`injection`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`csrf`,language:`en`,title:`Cross-site request forgery`,description:`State-changing requests are accepted without a token or other check that they come from the application itself.`,impact:`A malicious site visited by a logged-in user can make actions on their behalf.`,remediation:`- Require an anti-CSRF token for state-changing requests and set cookies with SameSite.`,references:[`WSTG-SESS-05`],cweIds:[`CWE-352`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`session`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`clickjacking`,language:`en`,title:`Clickjacking: page can be framed`,description:`Pages with sensitive actions can be embedded in frames by other sites.`,impact:`An attacker can trick users into clicking hidden controls of the application.`,remediation:`- Send Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors (or X-Frame-Options) to forbid framing by other origins.`,references:[`WSTG-CLNT-09`],cweIds:[`CWE-1021`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`headers`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`cors-misconfiguration`,language:`en`,title:`Permissive cross-origin resource sharing`,description:`The application allows cross-origin requests with credentials from origins it does not trust (for example by reflecting any Origin).`,impact:`A malicious site can read responses meant for the logged-in user, including personal data and tokens.`,remediation:`- Allow credentials only for an explicit list of trusted origins; never reflect the Origin header or allow "null".`,references:[`WSTG-CLNT-07`],cweIds:[`CWE-942`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`headers`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`verbose-errors`,language:`en`,title:`Verbose error messages`,description:`Errors return technical details such as stack traces, queries, file paths or software versions.`,impact:`The details help an attacker understand the application and refine other attacks.`,remediation:`- Show users generic error messages and keep the details in server logs.`,references:[`WSTG-ERRH-01`],cweIds:[`CWE-209`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`idor`,language:`en`,title:`Insecure direct object reference`,description:`Objects are accessed by an identifier from the request without checking that the user may access that object.`,impact:`By changing the identifier, a user can read or change data of other users.`,remediation:`- Check authorisation for every object on the server, based on the logged-in user.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHZ-04`,`A01:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-639`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`api`,`authorization`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`missing-function-authorization`,language:`en`,title:`Missing authorisation on functions`,description:`Functions meant for privileged users can be called by users without those privileges, for example by requesting their URL or API endpoint directly.`,impact:`Users can perform administrative or other restricted actions.`,remediation:`- Enforce authorisation on the server for every function, denying by default.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHZ-02`,`A01:2021`],cweIds:[`CWE-862`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`api`,`authorization`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`privilege-escalation-web`,language:`en`,title:`Vertical privilege escalation`,description:`A user can change their own role or permissions, or reach data reserved to higher roles.`,impact:`The user gains administrative control of the application.`,remediation:`- Never take roles or permissions from user-supplied data; check them on the server for each request.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHZ-03`],cweIds:[`CWE-266`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`authorization`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`mass-assignment`,language:`en`,title:`Mass assignment`,description:`The application binds request fields directly to internal objects, including fields the user should not set.`,impact:`A user can change protected properties, such as their role, price or account owner.`,remediation:`- Bind only an explicit list of allowed fields for each operation.`,references:[`WSTG-INPV-20`],cweIds:[`CWE-915`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`api`,`authorization`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`username-enumeration`,language:`en`,title:`Username enumeration`,description:`Login, registration or password reset respond differently for existing and non-existing accounts.`,impact:`An attacker can build a list of valid users to target password guessing and phishing.`,remediation:`- Return the same message, status and timing whether or not the account exists.`,references:[`WSTG-IDNT-04`],cweIds:[`CWE-204`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`no-bruteforce-protection`,language:`en`,title:`No protection against password guessing`,description:`The login does not limit repeated failed attempts through lockout, delays or other controls.`,impact:`Attackers can guess passwords automatically, including with lists of leaked credentials.`,remediation:`- Limit and slow down failed attempts per account and per source, and offer multi-factor authentication.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHN-03`],cweIds:[`CWE-307`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`weak-password-policy`,language:`en`,title:`Weak password policy`,description:`The application accepts short or common passwords.`,impact:`Weak passwords are easily guessed or found in leaked password lists.`,remediation:`- Require a sensible minimum length, reject known breached and common passwords, and offer multi-factor authentication.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHN-07`],cweIds:[`CWE-521`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`missing-mfa`,language:`en`,title:`No multi-factor authentication on a sensitive service`,description:`A sensitive service, such as remote access, email or administration, can be used with a password alone.`,impact:`A stolen or guessed password is enough to access the service.`,remediation:`- Require multi-factor authentication, preferably phishing-resistant, for the service.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-308`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`auth-bypass`,language:`en`,title:`Authentication bypass`,description:`Protected functionality can be reached without authenticating, for example through an alternative path or by altering a parameter.`,impact:`An unauthenticated attacker gains access to functions or data meant for logged-in users.`,remediation:`- Enforce authentication centrally on the server for every protected route, denying by default.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHN-04`],cweIds:[`CWE-288`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`session-fixation`,language:`en`,title:`Session fixation`,description:`The session identifier is not renewed when the user logs in.`,impact:`An attacker who sets a known session identifier in the victim's browser can use the session after the victim logs in.`,remediation:`- Issue a new session identifier at login and at every change of privilege.`,references:[`WSTG-SESS-03`],cweIds:[`CWE-384`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`session`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`session-expiration`,language:`en`,title:`Insufficient session expiration`,description:`Sessions stay valid for a long time without activity, or remain valid after logout.`,impact:`A session token that is stolen or left on a shared device can be used long after the user stopped.`,remediation:`- Expire sessions after inactivity and after an absolute time, and invalidate them on the server at logout.`,references:[`WSTG-SESS-07`],cweIds:[`CWE-1472`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`session`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`cookie-no-secure`,language:`en`,title:`Session cookie without the Secure attribute`,description:`A sensitive cookie is set without the Secure attribute, so the browser also sends it over plain HTTP.`,impact:`An attacker on the network can capture the cookie by luring the browser to an HTTP URL of the site.`,remediation:`- Set Secure on every sensitive cookie and serve the site only over HTTPS.`,references:[`WSTG-SESS-02`],cweIds:[`CWE-614`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`session`,`cookies`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`cookie-no-httponly`,language:`en`,title:`Session cookie without the HttpOnly attribute`,description:`A sensitive cookie is readable by script because it lacks the HttpOnly attribute.`,impact:`If any cross-site scripting exists, the session cookie can be stolen.`,remediation:`- Set HttpOnly on session cookies and other cookies script does not need.`,references:[`WSTG-SESS-02`],cweIds:[`CWE-1004`],defaultSeverity:`low`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`session`,`cookies`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`jwt-signature`,language:`en`,title:`JWT signature not properly verified`,description:`The application accepts JSON Web Tokens whose signature is missing, uses the "none" algorithm, or is checked with a key or algorithm chosen by the token itself.`,impact:`An attacker can forge tokens and act as any user.`,remediation:`- Verify signatures with a fixed algorithm and key on the server, and reject unsigned tokens.`,references:[`RFC 8725`],cweIds:[`CWE-347`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`api`,`authentication`,`session`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`password-reset-flaw`,language:`en`,title:`Weak password reset mechanism`,description:`The password reset relies on guessable tokens, tokens that do not expire, or information that others can know.`,impact:`An attacker can take over accounts by resetting their passwords.`,remediation:`- Use long random single-use tokens with a short lifetime, sent only to the verified channel of the user.`,references:[`WSTG-ATHN-09`],cweIds:[`CWE-640`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`authentication`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`hardcoded-credentials`,language:`en`,title:`Hard-coded credentials or secrets`,description:`Credentials, keys or tokens are embedded in source code, client-side code or configuration shipped with the application.`,impact:`Anyone with access to the code or the client can use the secret to reach the systems it protects.`,remediation:`- Remove the secret, rotate it, and load secrets at run time from a protected store.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-798`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`secrets`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`plaintext-password-storage`,language:`en`,title:`Passwords stored in plain text or reversibly`,description:`Passwords are stored in plain text, with reversible encryption, or with a fast unsalted hash.`,impact:`If the store is read, every password is exposed and can be reused on other services.`,remediation:`- Store passwords with a slow salted algorithm designed for passwords, such as Argon2id, scrypt or bcrypt.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-256`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`secrets`,`cryptography`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`sensitive-data-exposure`,language:`en`,title:`Excessive data in responses`,description:`Responses include more data than the client needs, such as internal fields or other users' details.`,impact:`Users can read information they should not see, even if the interface does not display it.`,remediation:`- Return only the fields each client needs, defined per endpoint on the server.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-213`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`api`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`sensitive-data-in-url`,language:`en`,title:`Sensitive data in URLs`,description:`Session tokens, passwords or personal data are sent in the URL.`,impact:`URLs are kept in browser history, logs and proxies and may leak through the Referer header.`,remediation:`- Send sensitive values in the request body or headers, never in the URL.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-598`],defaultSeverity:`low`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`web`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`weak-crypto-storage`,language:`en`,title:`Weak cryptography protecting data`,description:`Data is protected with broken or weak algorithms, short keys or unsafe modes.`,impact:`An attacker who obtains the data may decrypt or forge it.`,remediation:`- Use current algorithms and modes (for example AES-GCM) with proper key management.`,references:[`WSTG-CRYP-04`],cweIds:[`CWE-327`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`cryptography`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`no-rate-limiting`,language:`en`,title:`No rate limiting on API or expensive operations`,description:`The API or an expensive operation accepts an unlimited number of requests from a client.`,impact:`Attackers can exhaust resources, run up costs or automate abuse such as scraping or guessing.`,remediation:`- Apply rate limits and quotas per client and per operation, and limit request sizes.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-770`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`api`,`denial-of-service`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`graphql-introspection`,language:`en`,title:`GraphQL introspection enabled in production`,description:`The production GraphQL endpoint answers introspection queries, revealing its whole schema.`,impact:`The schema shows every type, field and operation, which helps attackers find sensitive or unprotected ones.`,remediation:`- Disable introspection in production, and check authorisation on every resolver.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-497`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`api`,`information-disclosure`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`api-docs-exposed`,language:`en`,title:`API documentation or debug endpoints exposed`,description:`Interactive API documentation, debug or monitoring endpoints are reachable in production.`,impact:`They reveal internal operations and may allow actions or data access not meant for users.`,remediation:`- Remove debug endpoints from production and restrict documentation and monitoring to internal users.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-489`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`api`,`configuration`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`llmnr-nbtns`,language:`en`,title:`LLMNR and NetBIOS name resolution enabled`,description:`Hosts fall back to LLMNR or NetBIOS name resolution, which any machine on the network can answer.`,impact:`An attacker on the network can impersonate names and capture or relay authentication of users and services.`,remediation:`- Disable LLMNR and NetBIOS over TCP/IP through policy and make sure DNS resolves the names in use.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-923`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`active-directory`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`kerberoasting`,language:`en`,title:`Service accounts vulnerable to Kerberoasting`,description:`Accounts with service principal names have passwords that can be cracked offline from Kerberos service tickets that any domain user can request.`,impact:`Cracked service account passwords often grant elevated privileges in the domain.`,remediation:`- Use long random passwords or group managed service accounts, prefer AES encryption, and remove unneeded service principal names.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-521`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`active-directory`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`asrep-roasting`,language:`en`,title:`Accounts without Kerberos pre-authentication`,description:`Some accounts do not require Kerberos pre-authentication, so anyone can request data that is encrypted with their password.`,impact:`Their passwords can be cracked offline without any credentials.`,remediation:`- Require Kerberos pre-authentication for every account unless there is a documented need.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-522`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`active-directory`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`local-admin-reuse`,language:`en`,title:`Shared local administrator password`,description:`Several hosts use the same password for the local administrator account.`,impact:`Compromising one host gives administrative access to all the others with the same password.`,remediation:`- Give each host a unique, rotated local administrator password (for example with Windows LAPS).`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-521`],defaultSeverity:`critical`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H`},tags:[`windows`,`active-directory`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`excessive-privileges`,language:`en`,title:`Excessive privileges assigned to accounts`,description:`Users or service accounts hold more privileges than their role requires, such as membership of administrative groups.`,impact:`A compromise of any of these accounts gives an attacker broad control.`,remediation:`- Grant the least privilege needed, review privileged group membership regularly and separate administrative accounts.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-250`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`active-directory`,`authorization`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`cleartext-credentials-shares`,language:`en`,title:`Credentials in files on shares`,description:`Scripts, configuration files or documents on network shares contain passwords or keys readable by ordinary users.`,impact:`Any user, or an attacker with their access, can collect the credentials and reuse them.`,remediation:`- Remove the credentials, rotate them, and restrict share permissions to those who need them.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-312`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`windows`,`secrets`,`file-sharing`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`missing-patches`,language:`en`,title:`Missing security updates`,description:`The host lacks security updates published by its vendor.`,impact:`The vulnerabilities they fix may be exploited; the impact depends on each update and should be verified.`,remediation:`- Apply the missing updates and review the patch management process so that it covers this host.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1395`],defaultSeverity:`high`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`maintenance`,`windows`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`flat-network`,language:`en`,title:`Insufficient network segmentation`,description:`Systems of different trust levels share a network segment, or traffic between segments is not filtered.`,impact:`An attacker who compromises one system can reach many others directly, including sensitive ones.`,remediation:`- Segment the network by function and sensitivity and allow only the flows that are needed between segments.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-923`],defaultSeverity:`medium`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:L`},tags:[`network`,`architecture`],ruleIds:[],version:1},{id:`service-nonstandard`,language:`en`,title:`Unexpected service exposed`,description:`A service is listening that is not part of the documented role of the host, or on an unusual port.`,impact:`Unknown services are rarely maintained and widen the attack surface.`,remediation:`- Identify the owner of the service; disable it if it is not needed, or document and protect it.`,references:[],cweIds:[`CWE-1188`],defaultSeverity:`info`,cvss:{"3.1":`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N`,"4.0":`CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`},tags:[`network`,`exposure`],ruleIds:[`vnmap:service-unidentified`,`vnmap:service-nonstandard-port`,`vnmap:port-unique-in-network`,`vnmap:many-open-ports`],version:1}],i={format:e,version:1,language:`en`,templates:r};export{i as default,e as format,n as language,r as templates,t as version};